Window Generation
=================

Purpose
-------

Raw RF recordings contain millions of IQ samples, while the neural network
expects fixed-size inputs.

Window generation divides a long recording into smaller fixed-length segments.
Each segment becomes one independent training sample.

Pipeline
--------

Raw IQ Recording

↓

Window Generation

↓

Fixed-Size IQ Windows

↓

Neural Network

Terminology
-----------

Window Size
~~~~~~~~~~~

Window size is the number of consecutive IQ samples contained in a single
training example.

Current Value

    Window Size = 4096 IQ Samples

Example

Recording

[--------------------------------------------------------------]

↓

[====4096====][====4096====][====4096====]

Every generated window contains exactly 4096 complex IQ samples.

Stride
~~~~~~

Stride is the distance the window moves before generating the next window.

Current Value

    Stride = 2048 IQ Samples

Since the stride is smaller than the window size, neighbouring windows overlap.

Example

Window Size = 4096
Stride      = 2048

Window 1

[================]

Window 2

        [================]

Window 3

                [================]

The overlapping region contains 2048 shared IQ samples.

Current Configuration
---------------------

Window Size : 4096

Stride      : 2048

Overlap     : 50%

Reason for Choosing Window Size
-------------------------------

A window size of 4096 IQ samples was selected as the baseline configuration.

This value

* captures sufficient temporal RF information,
* provides fixed-size inputs for the CNN,
* fits comfortably into memory,
* generates a large number of training samples from each recording.

The window size is treated as a tunable hyperparameter and may be evaluated
experimentally in future work.

Reason for Choosing 50% Overlap
-------------------------------

RF transmissions are continuous and do not necessarily align with window
boundaries.

Using overlapping windows ensures that signal characteristics occurring near
the end of one window also appear near the beginning of the next.

Benefits include

* Reduced boundary information loss.
* Better representation of complete RF patterns.
* Increased number of training samples.
* Improved robustness to signal alignment.

Although overlapping windows increase preprocessing time and storage
requirements, they provide better coverage of the original recording and are
commonly evaluated in RF signal processing applications.

Data Leakage Prevention
-----------------------

Window generation is performed only after splitting recordings into

* Training
* Validation
* Testing

Correct Workflow

Raw Recordings

↓

Train / Validation / Test Split

↓

Window Generation

↓

Model Training

This prevents overlapping windows originating from the same recording from
appearing in different datasets.

Implementation
--------------

Function

    create_windows(iq, window_size, stride)

Input

* Complex IQ signal
* Shape: (N,)

Output

* Complex IQ windows
* Shape: (Number of Windows, Window Size)

Testing
-------

The implementation has been verified using

* DJI Inspire 2
* DJI Mavic Pro
* Wi-Fi
* LTE
* 5G NR

Validation includes

* Windows are generated successfully.
* Window size is correct.
* Output remains complex.
* Output is two-dimensional.
* Windows are generated for every dataset.